{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-05 14:45:03 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-05 21:45:03 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: 01a10c70-ca15-7cc2-bd7b-0359f5aa64fb\n\nThe P1 is resolved. `head.cljc:140-143` validates shape before destructuring. `well-formed?` checks map types and closed key sets inside its catch boundary (`:72-87`); `verify` retains its catch boundary (`:119-121`). Additional JVM probes covering sets, keywords, records, non-keyword keys, and sorted maps produced the expected results without throwing. The portable regression helper catches host-appropriate exceptions (`head_test.cljc:221-227`), so its assertions do not assume a JVM exception type.\n\nNo actionable findings.\n\n- Leaving invalid `floor` arguments unguarded is reasonable: the documented contract requires a sequence or nil (`head.cljc:23-25`). The guarantee concerns arbitrary channel traces with valid caller state.\n- Hydration recording observes the actual write: `dht_test.cljc:627` wraps the store returned by `dao.space.dht/local` (`dht.cljc:372`), which `yin.repl.dht/hydrated` calls at `:208`. Omitting hydration’s HEAD write would fail the assertion at `dht_test.cljc:659`. The internal-path coupling is localized and fails visibly if that structure changes.\n- All three hydration cases are checked, including disk HEAD preservation and reopening after refusal (`dht_test.cljc:657-697`). Running the next round after reopening adds restart coverage; direct continuation after hydration is supported by `hydrated` calling `index/rehydrate` (`yin.repl.dht:210`).\n- The design amendments match the Architect’s concrete ruling, including hydration’s first-write exception, startup deposit, sequence bound, and revised stop rule (`yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md:224-250,276-281,313-316,575-580,958-983`). No contradictory requirement found.\n- No new P0–P2 found in the remaining uncommitted changes. Node and Dart behavior remains pending their lanes.\n\nready to commit once the Node and Dart lanes pass"}}
